GPLv2 and GPLv3-or-later are materially different and mutually incompatible
terms, so item 3 is a **separate licensing act, not a restatement of item 1**.
It is nonetheless a permitted one, and for the same reason this project's own
licensing is permitted: MIT allows redistribution under other terms, the GPL
included, so long as the MIT notice is retained.

This project distributes under GPL-3.0-or-later on that basis — the MIT grant
covering `wsproxy.js`. It does not rest on inheriting either upstream GPL
notice. See LICENSE for the full text.

